.git/
.github/
# csrc/ is a build input, not payload: aiter JIT-compiles its modules from these
# sources on first call. Excluding py_itfs_cu cost module_fmha_v3_fwd its
# asm_mha_fwd.cu, and the prebuilt .so then loaded with fmha_v3_fwd undefined
# and took down every attention forward; ck_gemm*/ also matched
# ck_gemm_a4w4_blockscale. Together they are ~1.3 MB, so there is nothing to
# save here.
third_party/aiter/aiter/jit/build/
# Host-built extensions. They are ABI-bound to the host torch, and a stale one
# is worse than none: aiter loads whatever .so is already sitting here instead
# of building, so a July module_aiter_core.so reaches the image and fails on
# the MlaVersion enum that postdates it.
third_party/aiter/aiter/jit/*.so
third_party/aiter/op_tests/
third_party/aiter/benchmarks/
third_party/aiter/docker/
# Run artifacts, 14 GB of them, and the COPY carries the whole context into
# every layer that has one: they made the base image 40 GB and the qwen3 image
# 55 GB. Nothing here is a build or runtime input — the launchers bind-mount a
# results dir over RESULTS_ROOT.
examples/*/results/
examples/*/wandb/
wandb/
outputs/
runs/
**/*.pt.trace.json
**/events.out.tfevents.*

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
.claude/
*.log
examples/dsv4/.bootstrap-build/tilelang/
examples/dsv4/miles_compat/
